# Veripsa release gate (auto-discovered). One gate per file -> two PRs adding gates add two FILES, never a
# shared line -> no false merge conflict on registration. register_gate is defined in run_gates.sh.
# Format: register_gate <test> <marker> <name> <ok_blurb> <desc> [tail]
register_gate "tests/test_prodtest_coupling_guard.py" "PROD-TEST COUPLING GUARD GATE: PASS" "prod->test call-coupling guard (false-coupling fix)" "prod->test call-coupling guard (audit r3 false-coupling fix): _claim_adjacency kept an import-UNCONFIRMED call coupling when the called name had a SINGLE definer (the unambiguous-recall rule) -- but a ubiquitous receiver/method name (.pop()/.end()/.is_a?/.Encode()) that a TEST file happens to define ONCE, called from a PRODUCTION file, is a coincidental name match (production code does not depend on a test file). Measured 8-40 such IMPOSSIBLE prod->test couplings/repo on axios/gin/sinatra. The fix adds a PROD->TEST asymmetry guard on out_adj/in_adj via core._is_test_path (test/spec/examples SEGMENTS + _test./.test./test_ prefix/_spec./.spec. BASENAMES + CamelCase Tests./Specs. case-sensitively, so latest.java/contest.py/manifest.py are NOT false-matched): drop a single-definer import-unconfirmed coupling whose DEFINER is a test file and whose CALLER is not. RECALL-SAFE -- import-confirmed links survive, prod->prod single-definer survives (the existing recall rule, still GREEN in false_coupling_precision), and test->test survives (two tests on one fixture coordinate). content-free. Proven on the live main_impact_surface: prod->test dropped (clear), prod->prod kept (warn), test->test kept (warn)" "prod->test false call-coupling dropped (a ubiquitous method name a test defines once no longer couples a production file to that test); prod->prod + test->test + import-confirmed all preserved; content-free, recall-safe" 24
